# Refactor Prompt System to Flattened TMP Prefab

The goal is to restore the dynamic pooling system for prompts (Interact, Pickup, Examine) in [AKUIManager](file:///home/tory/Documents/Code/unity/HorrorHouse/Assets/Scripts/Adventure%20Puzzle%20Kit%20v1.7.1/Core/AKUIManager.cs#21-1493). Instead of toggling static scene objects (which the user deleted), we will instantiate/enable prompt prefabs from a pool. These prefabs will have a single "flattened" TMP component displaying the combined "Key + Action" text.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Prefab Requirement**: Ensure `AKUIManager.promptPrefab` is assigned in the Inspector. This prefab should have a single `TextMeshProUGUI` component in its hierarchy (on root or child) to receive the text.
>
> **Scene Cleanup**: Remove any remaining references to the old static `interactPromptContainer`, `pickupPromptContainer`, etc., in the Inspector if they persist, or leave them null.

## Proposed Changes

### [Core] AKUIManager.cs

#### [MODIFY] [AKUIManager.cs](file:///home/tory/Documents/Code/unity/HorrorHouse/Assets/Scripts/Adventure%20Puzzle%20Kit%20v1.7.1/Core/AKUIManager.cs)

1.  **Restore Pooling Logic ([UpdatePromptsUI](file:///home/tory/Documents/Code/unity/HorrorHouse/Assets/Scripts/Adventure%20Puzzle%20Kit%20v1.7.1/Core/AKUIManager.cs#405-411) & Helpers)**:
    - Re-implement the body of [UpdatePromptsUI](file:///home/tory/Documents/Code/unity/HorrorHouse/Assets/Scripts/Adventure%20Puzzle%20Kit%20v1.7.1/Core/AKUIManager.cs#405-411) to:
        - Return current children of `promptContainer` to the pool.
        - Dequeue (or instantiate) new prompts from `promptPool` based on the input list.
        - **Flattening**: Find the *single* `TextMeshProUGUI` component on the prefab and set its text to `"{Key} {Label}"`.
    - Ensure [PrewarmPromptPool](file:///home/tory/Documents/Code/unity/HorrorHouse/Assets/Scripts/Adventure%20Puzzle%20Kit%20v1.7.1/Core/AKUIManager.cs#395-404) and [GetPooledPrompt](file:///home/tory/Documents/Code/unity/HorrorHouse/Assets/Scripts/Adventure%20Puzzle%20Kit%20v1.7.1/Core/AKUIManager.cs#412-424) are working as intended (already present but check logic).

2.  **Refactor [SetHighlightName](file:///home/tory/Documents/Code/unity/HorrorHouse/Assets/Scripts/Adventure%20Puzzle%20Kit%20v1.7.1/Core/AKUIManager.cs#427-459)**:
    - This method currently toggles static containers (`interactPromptContainer`, etc.). We will rewrite it to use the dynamic pooling system.
    - **Strategy**: Construct a list of temporary [Prompt](file:///home/tory/Documents/Code/unity/HorrorHouse/Assets/Scripts/Adventure%20Puzzle%20Kit%20v1.7.1/Core/AKUIManager.cs#412-424) data based on the bool arguments (`showInteractPrompt`, `showPickupPrompt`, etc.) and call [UpdatePromptsUI](file:///home/tory/Documents/Code/unity/HorrorHouse/Assets/Scripts/Adventure%20Puzzle%20Kit%20v1.7.1/Core/AKUIManager.cs#405-411) (or equivalent logic) to display them.
        - If `showInteractPrompt` is true -> Add "E Interact" to list.
        - If `showPickupPrompt` is true -> Add "E Pickup" to list.
        - If `showExaminePrompt` is true -> Add "Q Inspect" to list.
    - Pass this list to [UpdatePromptsUI](file:///home/tory/Documents/Code/unity/HorrorHouse/Assets/Scripts/Adventure%20Puzzle%20Kit%20v1.7.1/Core/AKUIManager.cs#405-411) so the UI refreshes with the correct dynamic prompts.
    - *HighlightName* logic remains separate (keeps using `highlightNameCanvas`), as that seems to be a distinct UI element (the name of the item), not a button prompt.

3.  **Cleanup**:
    - Remove usages of `interactPromptContainer`, `pickupPromptContainer`, `examinePromptContainer`, `interactPromptTextUI`, `pickupPromptTextUI`, etc.
    - These fields can be kept serialized but unused (or deleted if we want to be clean, user seems to have deleted the objects anyway).

## Verification Plan

### Manual Verification
1.  **Editor**: Assign the new flattened TMP prefab to [AKUIManager](file:///home/tory/Documents/Code/unity/HorrorHouse/Assets/Scripts/Adventure%20Puzzle%20Kit%20v1.7.1/Core/AKUIManager.cs#21-1493) -> `Prompt Prefab`.
2.  **Play Mode**:
    - **Move Overlay**: Look at an interactable object.
    - **Result**: [SetHighlightName](file:///home/tory/Documents/Code/unity/HorrorHouse/Assets/Scripts/Adventure%20Puzzle%20Kit%20v1.7.1/Core/AKUIManager.cs#427-459) is called. It generates a list of prompts (e.g. "E Interact"). [UpdatePromptsUI](file:///home/tory/Documents/Code/unity/HorrorHouse/Assets/Scripts/Adventure%20Puzzle%20Kit%20v1.7.1/Core/AKUIManager.cs#405-411) is called. A prompt prefab is spawned/enabled from pool. Text says "E Interact".
    - **Transition**: Look away. Prompts return to pool.
    - **Multiple Prompts**: (If applicable) Verify multiple prompts stack/layout correctly if `promptContainer` has a layout group (Vertical/Horizontal).
    - **Box Inspection**: Verify collecting items shows "E Collect" (Pickup prompt).
